  PrefabRemaps:
    []
  Name: Text
  Enabled: true
  RenderOrder: 11
  StretchMode: Stretch
  VerticalAlignment: Center
  HorizontalAlignment: Left
  MeshShadowMode: None
  ShadowColor: {x: 1.000000, y: 1.000000, z: 1.000000, w: 1.000000}
  ShadowDensity: 1.000000
  Text: |-
    SnapDecorators is a TypeScript library, not a visual effect: decorators bind lifecycle events, inject components and memoize getters, so scripts need less boilerplate.
    The Examples script here prints a line for each decorator-bound event: start, enable, an update every 60 frames with frame count and FPS, late update, and destroy. Follow it in the logs while the Lens runs.
  CustomMaterial: !<reference> 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
  Editable: false
  ShowEditingPreview: true
  TouchHandler: !<reference> 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
